  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To find the percentage of sales that came from sunflower bouquets:\n\n1. Divide the number of sunflower bouquets by the total bouquets sold:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{12}{50}=0.24\n   \\]\n\n2. Convert the decimal to a percentage:\n   \\[\n   0.24 \\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "No problem—the wording can be corrected to:\n\n**Faraday owns a flower shop. The shop sold 50 bouquets during the week, including 12 sunflower bouquets.**\n\nThe percentage is still:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\%=24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average per day}=\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. Individual sunflowers cost **$3 each**. To calculate the revenue from individual sunflowers, we would need to know how many individual sunflowers Faraday sold.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days:\n\n- **Individual sunflowers:**  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$26 \\times 3}{\\$3}=\\frac{\\$78}{\\$3}=26\n  \\]\n  So Faraday sold **26 individual sunflowers**.\n\n- **Bouquets:**  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$56 \\times 3}{\\$8}=\\frac{\\$168}{\\$8}=21\n  \\]\n  So Faraday sold **21 bouquets**.\n\nTherefore, Faraday sold:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers and }21\\text{ bouquets}}\n\\]\n\nThe exact total number of sunflowers cannot be determined unless we know how many sunflowers are in each bouquet.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days:\n\n- Individual sunflowers:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{26\\text{ dollars/day}\\times 3}{3\\text{ dollars/sunflower}}=26\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{56\\text{ dollars/day}\\times 3}{8\\text{ dollars/bouquet}}=21\\text{ bouquets}\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in bouquets:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\nTotal sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With individual sunflowers selling for **$2 each**:\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$26 \\times 3}{\\$2}=\\frac{\\$78}{\\$2}=39\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$56 \\times 3}{\\$8}=21\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in those bouquets:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\n  \\]\n\nTotal sunflowers sold:\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
